{
  "$comment": "Machine-readable source list for docs/references (ROADMAP M0-06). Images are official Steam store screenshots, used for critic comparison only and never shipped or committed (see .gitignore). Fetch with `pnpm refs:fetch`; SOURCES.md is generated from this file.",
  "size": {
    "width": 1280,
    "height": 720
  },
  "styleSelection": [
    "Sources: the six ROADMAP M0-06 titles, official Steam store screenshots only. For Jackbox, only Quiplash 3 from The Jackbox Party Pack 7: its sculpted-clay art direction fits research 03 (\"toy-real\" clay, \"nothing fully saturated\", \"avoid neon\"); the other packs and the pack's other games are flat vector or neon.",
    "The frame shows play: the game world, or for the party game an in-round screen (prompt, answers, vote). Excluded: title or logo cards, character or splash art, menus and settings or filter grids, and marketing overlays (stickers, stars).",
    "No tool UI over the subject: build gizmos, selection brackets, radial menus, pickers, lighting widgets and phone-camera overlays exclude a frame. A thin HUD or toolbar strip along one edge is allowed, since it is part of the shipped look.",
    "Day, golden-hour or dusk lighting only; night and uncoloured render modes are excluded. The board anchors the default Play look (research 03: golden hour \"is what makes everything look good\"); night modes are judged against the golden later.",
    "Pick the first 2 qualifying screenshots per source in the store page's published order (appdetails order, recorded in each note). Two per source is the largest equal count every source can meet (Tiny Glade has exactly two qualifying shots), so no single style dominates the leave-one-out contact sheet.",
    "Frames are never swapped because of a calibration score. A shortfall is fixed in the rubric anchors (ROADMAP M0-06 Accept)."
  ],
